reward text Forever's goblin quartermasters: gear for levels 20 to 50 at Friendly and Honored
collects 274024, 274022, 274023, 274021, 276199

# Built from Forever's data: the quest rows that pay the whole Cartel (header faction 169: Zapped Giants 7003
# and Fuel for the Zapping 7721, 150 each; Again With the Zapped Giants 7725 and Refuel for the Zapping 7726, 25
# each, repeatable; Tinkee Steamboil's chain 4726/4810, her Rookery quests 4734/4735 named only; The Gordok Ogre
# Suit 5518/5519, named only, and Free Knot 5525/7429 in Dire Maul), Forever's reputation values from its quest
# pages, the quest and kill rows of the four town factions (Booty Bay 21, Gadgetzan 369, Ratchet 470, Everlook
# 577), the drop and spawn data for the residue, cores, shackle keys
# and essences, and the five quartermasters Forever added with their items' standing and price from Forever's
# client item table (Winklespark 265574, Gezzy Gunkgear 265575, Rettrick 265576, Zippie Fizzbolt 265577, Friz
# Frazzlespark 255897). Forever's client faction table starts every town at Neutral 500 and gives Booty Bay,
# Gadgetzan, Ratchet, Everlook and Powderfuse the same parent (the Cartel) with the Classic share rules: a quest
# for the Cartel pays every town in full, and a gain with one town gives half as much to the others (losses
# too). Neutral 500 to Revered is 20,500 reputation per town, to Exalted 41,500.
# Kill caps: a capped kill pays up to the top of its last standing and no further (Southsea pirates: to the
# end of Honored; Wastewander and Bloodsail pirates: to the end of Neutral). Zorbin's repeatables (level 55) and
# Knot's quests (level 60) are never cut for level. Forever's world data lets the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900 take
# only Black and Scalding Broodlings, and drops the residue, the cores and the Chillwind horns only while their
# quest is in the log; the client item table gives the Ultra-Shrinker a two-hour life and lets you carry one
# Gordok Shackle Key at a time.
# ASSUMED: Powderfuse shares the Cartel's reputation like the four Classic towns (Forever's client data puts it
# in the same group; it has no quests or kills of its own in Forever's data). In-game check: does Powderfuse rise
# with a Zapped Giants turn-in?
# INGAME: grey-mob kill rep (Classic: about a fifth). Lost Rigger Cove's pirates are grey from level 56.
# INGAME: grey-quest rep. In Classic a quest paid full only while at most 5 levels below you, then a fifth less
# per level down to a fifth; a Forever beta report says quests paid in full at any level.
# The trinkets' use effects are not in the client tables we have: they are described by their stats.

step Zorbin Fandazzle
  tip Five goblin towns share one reputation family, the Steamwheedle Cartel: Ratchet, Booty Bay, Gadgetzan, Everlook and Forever's new Powderfuse in the Riverglades. Everyone starts each at Neutral (500 into it). A gain with one town gives the others half as much; a quest for the Cartel itself, like Zorbin's, pays every town in full. Losses spread the same way: a Booty Bay Bruiser or any goblin of the towns costs 125 (half that with the other towns), and Bloodsail Buccaneers reputation is earned only that way. Zorbin camps on the road through central Feralas and works for anyone, even players the goblins hate. His first two quests are level 48: in Classic they paid less once you were 6 or more levels above them (a fifth at 57 and up), but they open his repeatables, which are level 55 and pay in full at 60.
  accept 7003                         -- Zapped Giants: 150 to every town
  accept 7721                         -- Fuel for the Zapping: 150 to every town

step Zapped giants
  tip Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker on a living giant (Land Walker, Cliff Giant, or a Shore, Deep or Wave Strider, level 47-50) and it shrinks into a zapped version; kill that for its Miniaturization Residue, one every time. The Land Walkers and Cliff Giants in the north-west hills are the thickest; the striders walk the coast and the shallows. The shrinker lasts two hours: if it runs out, abandon the quest and take it again.
  goto 37.8,22.0 "Land Walkers and Cliff Giants"
  goto 36.4,34.0 "Shore and Deep Striders"
  goto 44.3,46.6 "Wave Striders"
  goto 45.1,58.0 "Striders on the south coast"
  loop
  use 18904 optional @37.8,22.0       -- Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker, on a living giant
  collect 18956 x15 quest 7003.1      -- Miniaturization Residue, from the zapped giants

step Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays
  tip The Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays (level 47-49) drift along the Forgotten Coast and in the shallows below the giants: about half drop a Water Elemental Core.
  goto 34.4,35.6 "Forgotten Coast"
  goto 44.5,52.5 "the south coast"
  loop
  collect 18958 x10 quest 7721.1      -- Water Elemental Core: Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays

step Back to Zorbin
  tip From now on Zorbin offers Again With the Zapped Giants (10 residue) and Refuel for the Zapping (6 cores), again and again: 25 reputation with every town each time.
  turnin 7003
  turnin 7721

step Lost Rigger Cove, below 56
  when level<56
  zone Tanaris
  tip The Southsea pirates of Lost Rigger Cove (level 44-45) on the east coast of Tanaris give Gadgetzan 5 each up to the end of Honored, and the other towns half. Two quests at Steamwheedle Port pay 100 Gadgetzan each: Southsea Shakedown (10 of each pirate) and Pirate Hats Ahoy! (20 Southsea Pirate Hats, one in ten pirates). From level 56 the pirates are grey and pay little: skip this step then.
  accept 8366                         -- Security Chief Bilgewhizzle, Steamwheedle Port
  accept 8365                         -- Haughty Modiste
  kill 7855 x10 quest 8366.1
  kill 7856 x10 quest 8366.2
  kill 7857 x10 quest 8366.3
  kill 7858 x10 quest 8366.4
  collect 20519 x20 quest 8365.1      -- Southsea Pirate Hat
  turnin 8366
  turnin 8365

step Tinkee Steamboil
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Tinkee Steamboil, a goblin at Flame Crest in the north of the Burning Steppes, has a chain that pays every town 150 and Everlook 150 more. Use her Draco-Incarcinatrix 900 on a broodling, kill it while the device holds it, and pick up the Broodling Essence it leaves. The device takes only Black and Scalding Broodlings, not the Flamescale Broodlings of the west: Scalding Broodlings (level 53-54) roam just west and east of Flame Crest, Black Broodlings (51-52) the north-east corner of the zone, the thickest group. They are few and spread out: the path passes both and ends among the Black Broodlings.
  accept 4726                         -- Tinkee Steamboil
  goto 59.2,32.3 "Scalding Broodlings west of Flame Crest"
  goto 73.2,27.1 "Scalding Broodlings east of Flame Crest"
  goto 87.8,33.5 "Black Broodlings in the north-east"
  use 12284 optional @87.8,33.5       -- Draco-Incarcinatrix 900, on a Black or Scalding Broodling
  collect 12283 x8 quest 4726.1 @87.8,33.5 -- Broodling Essence, left by the broodlings
  turnin 4726                         -- 100 to every town
  accept 4808

step Everlook: Felnok Steelspring
  zone Winterspring
  tip Felnok Steelspring is in Everlook. The Chillwind Chimaeras (level 55-57) south-west of Everlook drop the horns one time in five.
  turnin 4808                         -- 50 Everlook
  accept 4809
  collect 12444 x8 quest 4809.1 @55.4,47.5 -- Uncracked Chillwind Horn: Chillwind Chimaeras
  turnin 4809                         -- 100 Everlook
  accept 4810

step Back to Tinkee
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Return to Tinkee gives 50 to every town. Her later quests, Egg Freezing (150 to every town) and Egg Collection (200), are done in the Rookery of Upper Blackrock Spire, a ten-player dungeon: take them up with your group.
  turnin 4810

step Dire Maul North: Knot Thimblejack
  when level>=57
  zone Feralas
  tip Knot Thimblejack sits shackled in Dire Maul North, the Gordok ogres' wing (a five-player dungeon from level 57: group up). Every Gordok Shackle Key frees him once: 150 to every town, and he is shackled again on your next run. Gordok ogres drop the keys (about one in fifteen; Guard Fengus one in seven): a full run of the wing usually brings one. His Gordok Ogre Suit pays 100 the first time and 50 after, for 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 8 Rugged Leather, 2 Rune Thread and the Ogre Tannin from the basket in the wing. Under 57 when you get here? Unskip this step later.
  level 57
  goto 59.2,45.1 "Dire Maul"
  collect 18250 optional @59.2,45.1   -- Gordok Shackle Key, Gordok ogres
  accept 5525 optional @59.2,45.1     -- Free Knot!: 150 to every town
  turnin 5525 optional @59.2,45.1
  accept 7429 optional @59.2,45.1     -- Free Knot!, again on every later run: 150
  turnin 7429 optional @59.2,45.1

step Every town to Friendly
  tip Neutral 500 to Friendly is 2,500 with each town. The quests above pay every town up to 700 (Zorbin's two 300, Tinkee's 150, the first Free Knot 150 and the first Ogre Suit 100; less when you are well above their level); Zorbin's repeatables do the rest, 25 to every town each: 10 residue (ten giants) or 6 cores (about twelve elementals). The towns' own quests count too, each giving the other towns half: Ratchet's in the Barrens (levels 10-25, about 4,300: the Samophlange chain 625, Mebok Mizzyrix's errands, the Wizzlecrank and Gilthares escorts 150 each), Booty Bay's in Stranglethorn, Arathi and the Badlands (30-50, about 6,500: the three OOX robot rescues 250 each, An OOX of Your Own 200, Stranglethorn Fever 200, Facing Negolash 200, the Sunken Treasure chain at Faldir's Cove), Gadgetzan's in Tanaris (43-55, about 3,000: the Divino-matic Rod 200, Wastewander Justice 100 each, the WANTED posters) and Everlook's in Winterspring (52-60, about 1,450: Donova Snowden's Winterfall chain, Umi's yeti quests). Forever adds a few low ones: A Simmering Storm and Stormy Potential in Durotar and WANTED: Bruuz (Ratchet 100 each), Important Heirlooms in Ironforge (Gadgetzan 100). In Classic they pay in full only while at most 5 levels below you; past that each level takes a fifth off, down to a fifth. Kills help while they are not grey, 5 each: Southsea pirates in the Barrens for Ratchet and in Tanaris for Gadgetzan and Stranglethorn's Venture Co. camps for Booty Bay, up to the end of Honored; Wastewander bandits for Gadgetzan and Bloodsail pirates for Booty Bay only up to the end of Neutral. Friendly opens each quartermaster's first gear.
  accept 7725 optional                -- Again With the Zapped Giants: 10 residue
  collect 18956 x10 optional          -- Miniaturization Residue
  turnin 7725 optional                -- 25 to every town
  accept 7726 optional                -- Refuel for the Zapping: 6 cores
  collect 18958 x6 optional           -- Water Elemental Core
  turnin 7726 optional                -- 25 to every town
  rep 470 Friendly                    -- Ratchet
  rep 21 Friendly                     -- Booty Bay
  rep 369 Friendly                    -- Gadgetzan
  rep 577 Friendly                    -- Everlook
  rep 2827 Friendly optional          -- Powderfuse

step Every town to Honored
  tip Friendly to Honored is 6,000: 240 of Zorbin's turn-ins, or 40 Free Knot runs, or a mix. Nothing can be saved up: residue and cores drop only while their quest is in your log, and you can carry one Gordok Shackle Key at a time, so hand each in before the next run. Honored opens each quartermaster's blue items.
  accept 7725 optional
  collect 18956 x10 optional
  turnin 7725 optional
  accept 7726 optional
  collect 18958 x6 optional
  turnin 7726 optional
  rep 470 Honored
  rep 21 Honored
  rep 369 Honored
  rep 577 Honored
  rep 2827 Honored optional

step Every town to Revered
  tip Honored to Revered is 12,000 more: 480 of Zorbin's turn-ins (4,800 residue) or 80 Free Knot runs. Revered opens the five cosmetic hats, the reason most players do this. Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10%.
  accept 7725 optional
  collect 18956 x10 optional
  turnin 7725 optional
  accept 7726 optional
  collect 18958 x6 optional
  turnin 7726 optional
  rep 470 Revered
  rep 21 Revered
  rep 369 Revered
  rep 577 Revered
  rep 2827 Revered optional

step Ratchet: Winklespark
  zone The Barrens
  tip Winklespark, Ratchet's quartermaster, by the docks. Friendly, level 20 gear: Quilted Cloak 41s (Stamina, Agility), Rumpled Kilt 54s (Stamina, spell power), Ratchet Wristwraps 34s (Intellect, Agility). Honored: Defective Samophlange, an off-hand, 66s (Intellect, Spirit); Barrens Basher, a one-handed mace, 1g 65s (Stamina, Strength). Revered: the Barrens Headband, a cosmetic hat, 2g.
  buy 274740 optional                 -- Quilted Cloak, Friendly
  buy 274741 optional                 -- Rumpled Kilt, Friendly
  buy 274742 optional                 -- Ratchet Wristwraps, Friendly
  buy 274743 optional                 -- Defective Samophlange, Honored
  buy 274744 optional                 -- Barrens Basher, Honored
  buy 274021 optional                 -- Barrens Headband, Revered

